{"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK14SetOrgSettingsV4cimdAA10CimdPolicyVSgvp","title":"cimd","symbolKind":"property","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cimd","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK10CimdPolicyV","text":"CimdPolicy","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/SetOrgSettings"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"T21.5 — defaulted, so an API client written before this task lands on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"enabled: false"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which is what every deployment did before client ID metadata documents existed (I1)."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"cimd"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CimdPolicy","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"CimdPolicy","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK10CimdPolicyV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/SetOrgSettings\/cimd","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/setorgsettings\/cimd"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/CimdPolicy":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"CimdPolicy"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CimdPolicy","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/cimdpolicy","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"CimdPolicy","abstract":[{"text":"Whether, and on what terms, a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_id"},{"text":" that is a URL is resolved by fetching the document","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it names (T21.5, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"draft-ietf-oauth-client-id-metadata-document"},{"text":"). # Why this is one nested","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"policy rather than nine fields Every field here is a term of a single decision — ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"do we","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fetch a stranger’s URL and make a client out of what comes back","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" — and none of them means","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"anything without [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::enabled"},{"text":"]. A tenant that states a CIMD posture states all of it; a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tenant that states none inherits its organization’s whole posture rather than half of one,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which is the only merge that cannot produce a combination neither party wrote. # The two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fields that can widen, and the seven that cannot [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::enabled"},{"text":"] and [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::allow_http"},{"type":"text","text":"]"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"ordered","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": a tenant may turn either off but never on, exactly as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dynamic_registration"},{"type":"text","text":" may only move down its ladder. Everything else names "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"this tenant’s","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"domains or "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"this tenant’s","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" bounds, and there is no sense in which one tenant’s list of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"trusted publishers is stricter than another’s — the same argument ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OidcPolicy"},{"type":"text","text":"] already"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"makes for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dcr_allowed_redirect_hosts"},{"type":"text","text":". # Every bound here is a security control"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::max_metadata_bytes"},{"type":"text","text":"], ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::min_cache_secs"},{"type":"text","text":"] and ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::max_cache_secs"},{"type":"text","text":"] are not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tuning knobs. They are, respectively, the ceiling on a read from an attacker-chosen URL, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"floor under how often that read may be repeated, and the ceiling on how long its result may"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be trusted. Each is clamped again in code against the three constants above, so a settings"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row written by hand cannot lift them."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"CimdPolicy"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/SetOrgSettings":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/setorgsettings","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/SetOrgSettings","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SetOrgSettings","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"SetOrgSettings","abstract":[{"text":"Input for setting organization-level security settings.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SetOrgSettings","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Ax